<title>USA: Allow CRP haying in North Plains, US senators ask.</title>
<headline>Allow CRP haying in North Plains, US senators ask.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department should allow haying on Conservation Reserve Program acreage in the northern plains, two U.S. senators said Thursday.</p>
<p>Tom Daschle of South Dakota, the Democratic leader in the Senate, and North Dakota Democrat Byron Dorgan said they had asked USDA to allow CRP haying in portions of North Dakota, South Dakota and Montana because of drought.</p>
<p>Haying and grazing usually are barred on CRP land.</p>
<p>&quot;It is extremely urgent the CRP be opened for haying as soon as possible,&quot; Dorgan said. Daschle said he was confident USDA &quot;will continue to be responsive to our needs.&quot;</p>
</text>
